message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Everettian Decoherence in Lean"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dalimier
    given-names: Bertrand
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    city: Nogent-sur-Marne
    country: FR
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2457-375X"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of finite projective-decomposition robustness results,
  including projector-commutator bounds, exact cut-envelope rigidity,
  quantitative two-cell stability with sharp asymptotic coefficients,
  continuous three-cell sharpness families, fixed-budget proof mechanisms,
  and a geometric diffuse 2m-cell family attaining the sharp 1/8
  complete-diffusion threshold. The formalization is finite-dimensional and
  algebraic; it does not introduce time dynamics, Hamiltonians, open-system
  evolution, or a theorem of physical decoherence.
keywords:
  - quantum foundations
  - projective decompositions
  - projector commutators
  - rigidity
  - stability
  - sharpness
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-23
